@@ BE4 | Hybrid
What is the key difference between the issue log and the risk register?
A) Issues are current problems; risks are uncertain future events
B) The issue log is for predictive work; the risk register is for agile work
C) The issue log is confidential, while the risk register is shared publicly
D) There is no difference; they are two names for the same document
= A
? Issues have already happened and need resolution; risks may or may not happen and need analysis and responses.

@@ BE4 | Agile
Five agile teams frequently block each other because of unrecognised dependencies. What practice would help most?
A) A visible dependency board reviewed regularly by team representatives
B) A rule that each team must work independently of all the other teams
C) A monthly report on blocked items that is sent to senior management
D) A single team that does all of the work requiring coordination
= A
? Making dependencies visible and reviewing them regularly (for example, in a scrum of scrums) prevents blocks.

@@ BE4 | Predictive
The owner of an important issue has not responded for two weeks, and the issue is delaying work. What should the project manager do?
A) Follow up directly and, if needed, agree a new owner via their manager
B) Close the issue, since its owner has stopped responding to messages
C) Resolve the issue personally without informing the current owner
D) Wait until the owner has finished their other work and returns
= A
? Issues need active ownership; the PM follows up and, if necessary, reassigns ownership through the proper channel.

@@ BE4 | Agile | multi
