@@ BE5 | Hybrid
A Monte Carlo cost simulation shows a 50% probability that the project will cost $4.2 million or less, and an 80% probability for $4.6 million. The organisation's policy is to budget at 80% confidence. What should the project budget be?
A) $4.6 million
B) $4.2 million
C) $4.4 million
D) $5.0 million
= A
? The P80 value from the simulation is $4.6 million, which meets the policy's confidence requirement.

