@@ BE5 | Predictive | fill
Option A costs $80,000 and has a 20% chance of an extra $50,000 cost. What is the expected cost of option A? (Answer in dollars.)
= $90,000
? Expected cost = 80,000 + 0.20 × 50,000 = 80,000 + 10,000 = $90,000.

